course: dictionary
lesson: 11815
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is meant by looking at the words around it. This is context. «Mia put on her bikini and ran into the pool.» The clues are pool and ran, so bikini means a swimsuit.
explain: «The class read about Bikini Atoll, a group of islands in the Pacific Ocean.» The word atoll and the capital letters tell you this is a place, not clothing. A name with capital letters usually names one particular place or thing.
explain: When you are not sure which meaning fits, swap each one into the sentence. «Mia put on her island and ran into the pool» makes no sense, so the swimsuit meaning is the right one.
fact: A bikini is a two-piece swimsuit for women and girls, with a top and bottoms.
fact: Bikini Atoll is a group of islands in the Pacific Ocean.
fact: The USA tested nuclear bombs at Bikini Atoll, and history lessons link this to the 1940s and 1950s.
fact: The swimsuit was named after Bikini Atoll.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means.
exercise: «Sam packed a towel, sunscreen and a bikini for the beach.» What does bikini mean here? | A hat for the sun | *A two-piece swimsuit | A type of beach ball | A group of islands in the Pacific Ocean
exercise: Mia says bikini always means a group of islands. What should you tell her? | Yes, bikini always means islands | No, bikini means a sandwich | Yes, and it is also a type of shoe | *No, a bikini is a swimsuit, but Bikini Atoll is a group of islands
exercise: «The class read about Bikini Atoll, where nuclear bombs were tested.» Which clue shows that Bikini Atoll is a place? | The word read | The word class | *Capital letters and the word where | The word about and the word bombs
test: «Dad bought two bikini tops and one pair of bikini bottoms.» What does bikini mean here? | A kind of fish | *A two-piece swimsuit | A group of islands | A sports team
test: «The islands of Bikini Atoll are in the Pacific Ocean.» Which meaning fits this sentence? | A swimsuit | A type of bread | A football team | *A group of islands
exam: Why is a capital letter a useful clue when you meet bikini? | It means the sentence is a question | It shows the word is a verb | *It can show a name, such as Bikini Atoll | It shows the word always means a swimsuit
